## Job

Why: The app needs one place that says who acts.

An act names a calling: who answers, who does, who checks, and what is given first.
No calling, no run.
The hands are compute, model, and user.

## Hands

Why: Three hands, one calling.

Compute works from the rules and the books. It does not guess. A miss goes up.
The model drafts, and it asks compute for a cold boot of the book.
The user holds the desk and the risk. On this desk that user is the director.
`reply:` is the user only. The model records its work on `status:`. Compute writes that status.
Sign checks that a page is finished. Approve, lock, and promote stay with the user.
The calling is read from the command list.
An author on every section, the two user modes, and the shape of the local mode are still open.

